00:28:15.960 --> 00:28:16.880
You're in danger.

00:28:17.060 --> 00:28:18.770
We all are.

00:28:18.910 --> 00:28:20.600
But who?

00:28:20.860 --> 00:28:24.040
I hope for your sake you never find out.

00:28:39.630 --> 00:28:40.410
I'm Annabelle Lauren.

00:28:40.570 --> 00:28:41.350
Were you looking for something?

00:28:41.530 --> 00:28:42.950
Not exactly.

00:28:43.150 --> 00:28:43.890
Are you the doctor?

00:28:44.130 --> 00:28:44.830
No, no.

00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:45.660
I'm Lance Schroeder.

00:28:45.700 --> 00:28:46.260
The pilot.

00:28:46.780 --> 00:28:47.520
You've hurt yourself.

00:28:47.970 --> 00:28:49.830
Oh, it's just a bump on the head.

00:28:49.910 --> 00:28:53.110
Which is my room.

00:28:53.780 --> 00:28:54.620
I believe this is it.

00:28:56.350 --> 00:28:57.170
Thank you, Mrs. Lauren.

00:28:59.260 --> 00:28:59.860
Annabelle, I...

00:29:11.964 --> 00:29:14.724
You were with the young girl in the cellar. Why was she so upset?

00:29:15.484 --> 00:29:15.824
Watch it.

00:29:16.636 --> 00:29:19.036
And you don't look like the type to go around bumping his head.

00:29:19.740 --> 00:29:21.100
What really happened is...

00:29:21.852 --> 00:29:25.212
Well, Nora thought she saw a ghost, but I didn't see anything.

00:29:25.948 --> 00:29:26.808
She was just frightened.

00:29:27.516 --> 00:29:29.716
And mad at me, I think I kidded her about it.

00:29:31.372 --> 00:29:33.592
I wouldn't joke about anything else that happens here tonight.

00:29:34.316 --> 00:29:36.296
Now, don't tell me you're taking all this seriously.

00:29:37.516 --> 00:29:38.016
Aren't you?

00:29:38.572 --> 00:29:40.972
Well, I'd like to find out what hit me.

00:29:41.996 --> 00:29:43.996
Lens

00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:47.820
If I need help, me, I count on you.

00:29:50.188 --> 00:29:51.028
Sure, I guess so.

00:29:53.484 --> 00:29:55.664
Look, what's going on here, anyway? I mean...

00:29:55.820 --> 00:29:56.980
What is with this party, Biff?

00:29:57.140 --> 00:29:59.020
This is no party. He's planning something.

00:29:59.724 --> 00:29:59.884
Thank you.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.060
I wish I knew what it was.

00:30:03.160 --> 00:30:05.440
Must be pretty big if he's gonna lay out 50,000.

00:30:05.740 --> 00:30:06.820
The money doesn't mean anything.

00:30:07.980 --> 00:30:11.300
He has a reason for getting us all up here to this dreadful old house.

00:30:11.920 --> 00:30:13.620
Well, what for? He doesn't even know us.

00:30:14.590 --> 00:30:16.150
Maybe that's exactly why you're here.

00:30:17.630 --> 00:30:19.380
Well, can he get away with?

00:30:19.930 --> 00:30:22.690
Oh, he thinks that big money like his can get away with anything.

00:30:23.640 --> 00:30:25.420
You know, of course, that I'm his fourth wife.

00:30:26.820 --> 00:30:29.860
The first simply disappeared. The other two died.

00:30:31.404 --> 00:30:31.904
Lance.

00:30:33.100 --> 00:30:34.160
I don't want to join them.

00:30:37.100 --> 00:30:38.140
You mean he, uh...

00:30:38.140 --> 00:30:40.640
Oh, his doctor said they died of heart attacks.

00:30:41.868 --> 00:30:42.608
Two girls.

00:30:43.852 --> 00:30:44.652
In their 20s.

00:30:45.708 --> 00:30:46.708
Well, what can he do?

00:30:47.852 --> 00:30:49.852
My husband is sometimes insane with jealousy.

00:30:50.012 --> 00:30:51.052
Nothing matters to him then.

00:30:52.684 --> 00:30:53.404
Please be careful.

00:30:55.212 --> 00:30:55.712
hurt you.

00:30:57.868 --> 00:30:59.088
He would kill me if he could.

00:31:22.652 --> 00:31:23.292
all the fun.

00:31:25.052 --> 00:31:27.232
And he was almost killed by a falling chandelier.

00:31:27.352 --> 00:31:28.732
The pilot bashed his head in.

00:31:29.276 --> 00:31:29.996
Is he barely heard?

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.830
A Saturday night psychiatrist bandaged him up.

00:31:33.980 --> 00:31:35.440
Don't you want to go and console him?

00:31:35.540 --> 00:31:38.620
As you do most men in your fashion.

00:31:40.380 --> 00:31:41.380
You're so clever, Frederick.

00:31:42.420 --> 00:31:44.820
Yes, I lie awake nights wondering why I married you.

00:31:45.480 --> 00:31:46.460
It was rather a mistake.

00:31:46.860 --> 00:31:48.490
You didn't marry me, dear.

00:31:48.570 --> 00:31:49.170
I married you.

00:31:49.450 --> 00:31:50.650
Unpleasant, but no mistake.

00:31:52.940 --> 00:31:53.400
Hurry up.

00:31:54.170 --> 00:31:56.710
Frederick, for the last time, I'm not going to your party.

00:31:56.950 --> 00:31:59.790
For the last time, it's not my party.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:13.260
but yours and you are going. I am not. Are you ready? No. Are you ready, dear? Yes, am you.

00:32:14.370 --> 00:32:22.900
Adore me as much if I will come out. All you want to be is a lovely widow. It's almost time

00:32:22.900 --> 00:32:29.880
to lock up the house. Then your party will really begin. I wonder how it'll end.

00:32:50.860 --> 00:32:51.440
Midnight land.

00:32:52.480 --> 00:32:52.680
Okay.

00:32:53.410 --> 00:32:53.990
I'll be down in a minute.

00:33:02.250 --> 00:33:07.050
Your host, my dear. It's almost midnight, Nora.

00:33:07.450 --> 00:33:09.270
We're all going to get together down in the living room.

00:33:09.870 --> 00:33:11.620
All right, Mr. Lloyd. I'll be right down.

00:33:31.370 --> 00:33:31.550
Eh!

00:34:12.510 --> 00:34:13.730
with us before he kills you.

00:34:31.720 --> 00:34:53.740
stay here Nora what happened Jonas slides and his wife they've been caretakers

00:34:53.740 --> 00:34:58.450
here for years she's blind you stay here

00:35:02.170 --> 00:35:05.350
Doctor, it looks like we have a real case of hysteria in our hands.

00:35:06.230 --> 00:35:09.030
I think she's just a little upset, not hysterical.

00:35:16.460 --> 00:35:16.840
Good evening.

00:35:21.990 --> 00:35:22.290
My dear.

00:35:24.040 --> 00:35:24.700
It's my wife.

00:35:25.380 --> 00:35:26.260
These are our guests.

00:35:27.670 --> 00:35:29.460
Ruth Bridges, Dr. Trent.

00:35:30.250 --> 00:35:35.840
You know Watson Pritchard, of course, Nora Manning, and, uh, this is Lance Schroeder.

00:35:45.180 --> 00:35:45.640
Ten thousand.

00:35:45.640 --> 00:35:47.220
I don't care. He wants to kill me.

00:35:48.020 --> 00:35:49.100
Who wants to kill you?

00:35:50.330 --> 00:35:50.830
Your Lord.

00:35:52.520 --> 00:35:53.860
May I have your attention, please?

00:35:54.380 --> 00:35:58.200
I think you all remember the bargain we made about staying all night.

00:35:59.010 --> 00:35:59.910
Ten thousand dollars.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:06.660
If any of you don't survive, $50,000 will be divided amongst the rest of you.

00:36:07.280 --> 00:36:14.720
If I should die, be paid by my estate.

00:36:15.520 --> 00:36:20.660
When the door is locked from the outside by the caretakers, we'll all be forced to stay in this house until morning.

00:36:21.120 --> 00:36:24.500
If any of you decide not to stay, you must leave with the caretakers now.

00:36:24.940 --> 00:36:29.920
You won't have a chance to change your minds later, because there'll be no way to get out.

00:36:30.990 --> 00:36:31.810
I don't want to stay.

00:36:31.950 --> 00:36:32.190
Wait.

00:36:57.010 --> 00:36:57.370
Midnight?

00:36:57.470 --> 00:36:58.690
Yet who told them they could leave?

00:36:58.830 --> 00:36:59.970
They never leave before mid...

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:08.600
They've gone now. I was going to ask you whether you wanted to stay or not, but it seems that the caretakers have made the decision for you.

00:37:09.430 --> 00:37:16.750
We're all locked in now, but I don't want to stay. I'm sorry, my dear, but it's too late now. Darling,

00:37:17.590 --> 00:37:24.430
haven't you had enough of the silly game? Get some cars up here for these people and let them go home, but pay them first.

00:37:27.120 --> 00:37:29.180
This is your party, remember.

00:37:31.920 --> 00:37:35.120
In spite of my wife's faith in my ability to do the impossible,

00:37:36.230 --> 00:37:39.350
we will all have to stay in this house until 8 o'clock in the morning.

00:37:40.120 --> 00:37:44.840
But we have some party favors for you in these little coffins.

00:37:50.240 --> 00:37:54.270
My wife's idea, I must say, I think it's rather dangerous.

00:37:54.940 --> 00:37:57.380
I suppose you all know how to use one of these things,

00:37:57.540 --> 00:37:59.980
but in case you don't, you just...

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:03.800
Press down on this lever, with your thumb, and then pull the trigger.

00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:08.930
You see, they're loaded.

00:38:12.150 --> 00:38:14.250
These are no good against the dead, only the living.

00:38:17.260 --> 00:38:17.620
Doctor.

00:38:20.700 --> 00:38:21.000
Hands.

00:38:28.620 --> 00:38:28.900
Take it.

00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:41.370
Miss Bridgers, tea is yours, dear.

00:38:41.720 --> 00:38:42.480
I don't need it.

00:38:43.270 --> 00:38:43.970
It was your idea.

00:38:45.100 --> 00:38:47.720
Who knows you may want to use it on me before this night is over.

00:38:51.190 --> 00:38:52.330
Throw these guns away.

00:38:52.490 --> 00:38:53.630
They won't do you any good.

00:38:54.250 --> 00:38:57.520
I agree with Bridger on that board, although not for the same reason.

00:38:58.380 --> 00:38:59.060
Dr. Trent.

00:39:01.790 --> 00:39:04.910
Don't you approve of our little party favors?

00:39:06.690 --> 00:39:10.250
Suppose Nora had had a gun when she mistook the blind woman for a ghost.

00:39:10.840 --> 00:39:14.160
I don't think anyone else is going to walk around in total darkness.

00:39:15.090 --> 00:39:19.090
Oh, I'm sure we're not going to go running around the house shooting each other, aren't you?

00:39:19.870 --> 00:39:23.110
Who knows? Fear makes people do amazing things.

00:39:30.640 --> 00:39:34.100
You said your sister-in-law killed a man and a woman here and cut them up.

00:39:35.220 --> 00:39:38.200
You said they found hands and feet, but they never found any heads.

00:39:39.420 --> 00:39:40.840
Would you like to see one of those heads?

00:39:41.690 --> 00:39:43.290
Would you all like to see one of those heads?

00:39:44.180 --> 00:39:45.930
Well, then, just follow me.

00:39:54.760 --> 00:39:57.900
Darling, I really don't need this.

00:40:14.652 --> 00:40:15.492
in my suitcase.

00:40:15.996 --> 00:40:16.716
Just go look.

00:40:30.572 --> 00:40:31.572
What did he was in there?

00:40:32.268 --> 00:40:33.268
A woman's head!

00:40:33.580 --> 00:40:34.580
Nora.

00:40:34.636 --> 00:40:36.036
I think you're a little upset.

00:40:36.780 --> 00:40:37.900
Would you care for a sedative?

00:40:49.772 --> 00:40:51.772
Do you think it's alright to leave her by herself, Doctor?

00:40:52.300 --> 00:40:53.560
I wish she'd taken the sedative.

00:40:54.092 --> 00:40:56.012
What do you suppose she thought she saw?

00:40:56.176 --> 00:40:57.476
They're closing in on her.

00:40:57.708 --> 00:40:59.468
Look, Doc, I think somebody ought to stay with her.

00:41:00.090 --> 00:41:07.690
million people around her. If they wanted her, they'd get her. What if he's right? He's too

00:41:07.690 --> 00:41:12.300
drunk to know what he's talking about. I wonder. I'll join you in a minute.

00:41:19.250 --> 00:41:21.540
You think it would do any good if you went in and talked to her?

00:41:22.260 --> 00:41:24.460
Do you think there really was a head in her suitcase?

00:41:24.920 --> 00:41:26.420
I don't know.

00:41:27.140 --> 00:41:29.100
Something like that would put me right over the edge.

00:41:30.252 --> 00:41:33.332
Would you sort of stay up here, I mean, in case she needs help?

00:41:34.572 --> 00:41:35.192
All right.

00:41:35.884 --> 00:41:36.784
I'll be in my room.

00:41:37.228 --> 00:41:39.228
just cold

00:41:39.340 --> 00:41:39.620
Thanks.

00:41:51.852 --> 00:41:53.832
Are you sure there are only seven people in this house?

00:41:54.156 --> 00:41:54.716
Grazie a tutti.

00:41:55.148 --> 00:41:56.228
Except for the ghosts.

00:41:57.068 --> 00:41:58.148
I don't believe in ghosts.

00:41:59.308 --> 00:41:59.968
nor in frightening.

00:42:00.060 --> 00:42:04.780
In Nora's case, it's gone far enough. Perhaps too far.

00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:07.230
What do you suggest we do about it, Doctor?

00:42:07.880 --> 00:42:09.080
Don't frighten her any more.

00:42:32.910 --> 00:42:33.390
Nora.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:30.420
taking her.

00:43:31.244 --> 00:43:32.744
In a little while, she'll be one of them.

00:43:35.340 --> 00:43:36.180
Where's North?

00:43:38.028 --> 00:43:38.528
Where is she?

00:43:38.572 --> 00:43:39.192
It's too late.

00:43:39.724 --> 00:43:40.064
too late.

00:43:40.524 --> 00:43:41.824
You'll never find her again.

00:43:42.124 --> 00:43:44.364
Pritchard, if you know where she is, you better tell me now.

00:43:44.364 --> 00:43:46.084
She's gone. She's gone to them.

00:43:46.636 --> 00:43:48.196
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:44:55.950 --> 00:44:59.590
dead myself.

00:45:01.340 --> 00:45:01.900
Suicide.

00:45:33.580 --> 00:45:35.040
Please hide me. Please hide me.

00:45:35.330 --> 00:45:35.690
What's the matter?

00:45:46.400 --> 00:45:47.400
George killed me.

00:45:49.120 --> 00:45:51.560
He grabbed me and choked me and put me in that room.

00:45:52.540 --> 00:45:54.260
And then he went away and left me.

00:45:54.870 --> 00:45:55.130
Who?

00:45:56.150 --> 00:45:58.040
He thought I was dead.

00:45:58.760 --> 00:45:58.920
Who?

00:46:01.020 --> 00:46:01.820
Mr. Lord.

00:46:03.700 --> 00:46:04.860
Are you sure about this?

00:46:06.780 --> 00:46:09.860
I don't know. It was dark, but it must have been him.

00:46:11.580 --> 00:46:12.940
Has anybody seen you since he left you?

00:46:15.360 --> 00:46:18.160
I heard some people in that room, but I went by and nobody saw you.

00:46:20.960 --> 00:46:29.970
Lauren is dead. Lauren said she could be.

00:46:30.060 --> 00:46:32.900
It's suicide, but I think somebody killed her.

00:46:33.550 --> 00:46:33.810
Him?

00:47:12.540 --> 00:47:14.380
I'm sure you've come to the same conclusion I have.

00:47:15.020 --> 00:47:16.000
Yeah, I think so.

00:47:16.220 --> 00:47:17.920
Let's all have a meeting, discuss what to do.

00:47:19.370 --> 00:47:19.850
The living room?

00:47:20.540 --> 00:47:20.820
Okay.

00:47:36.750 --> 00:47:37.370
I've got to go downstairs.

00:47:38.450 --> 00:47:40.690
Now you lock yourself in here and don't let anybody know you're here.

00:47:41.860 --> 00:47:43.420
He thinks you're dead, he won't come here.

00:47:43.870 --> 00:47:45.050
And I'll get back as soon as I can.

00:47:46.620 --> 00:47:47.200
You'll be all right.

00:47:52.090 --> 00:47:52.630
If you have to.

00:49:00.284 --> 00:49:01.304
What are you doing in here?

00:49:01.544 --> 00:49:01.844
Weep.

00:49:02.268 --> 00:49:02.768
Don't we?

00:49:03.068 --> 00:49:05.068
What do you mean coming in here?

00:49:06.108 --> 00:49:07.348
I didn't want them to take her away.

00:49:07.932 --> 00:49:11.492
drunk. They will if you don't watch her. You're drunk. All right, out with it, Bridget. Why did

00:49:11.492 --> 00:49:14.232
you come into this room? I'm the only one who understands. Understands what?

00:49:15.708 --> 00:49:17.048
Your wife isn't there anymore.

00:49:18.300 --> 00:49:19.420
She's already joined them.

00:49:20.028 --> 00:49:22.048
Bridget, I've had enough of your spook talk.

00:49:22.556 --> 00:49:25.496
Get out, you sot, and don't come back into this room again.

00:50:00.188 --> 00:50:01.208
Where's what's her name?

00:50:02.684 --> 00:50:03.004
Nora.

00:50:04.956 --> 00:50:07.476
I didn't disturb her since I don't think this concerns her.

00:50:07.804 --> 00:50:08.464
No, you're right.

00:50:10.268 --> 00:50:10.888
Mr. Lauren.

00:50:12.060 --> 00:50:14.280
Isn't there some way we can get out of this house now?

00:50:15.644 --> 00:50:16.144
No.

00:50:16.572 --> 00:50:17.272
None at all.

00:50:18.076 --> 00:50:19.316
We could try breaking out.

00:50:19.612 --> 00:50:22.112
The only door to the outside is made of steel.

00:50:23.260 --> 00:50:25.860
The bars of the windows are set in solid stone.

00:50:27.612 --> 00:50:28.432
We gotta stay.

00:50:30.924 --> 00:50:32.424
I'm not afraid of your ghosts, Bridget.

00:50:35.724 --> 00:50:36.424
But I am afraid.

00:50:39.084 --> 00:50:43.004
When we came here a few hours ago, the only thing we had in common was the $10,000 we'd get.

00:50:43.948 --> 00:50:45.448
Now, however, we share something else.

00:50:46.892 --> 00:50:47.732
The death of Mrs. Lauren.

00:50:50.444 --> 00:50:51.164
So far tonight.

00:50:52.492 --> 00:50:54.832
One of us was almost killed by a falling chandelier.

00:50:56.268 --> 00:50:58.108
One of us was mysteriously slugged.

00:50:59.148 --> 00:50:59.988
One of us has been driven.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.600
into the brink of absolute hysteria.

00:51:03.580 --> 00:51:04.440
And one of us is dead.

00:51:06.780 --> 00:51:07.560
Were these accidents?

00:51:08.892 --> 00:51:09.492
Suicide?

00:51:10.908 --> 00:51:12.528
And we must stay here for six more hours.

00:51:12.988 --> 00:51:13.608
Six hours?

00:51:15.804 --> 00:51:16.524
Six of us.

00:51:18.812 --> 00:51:19.312
Time to know.

00:51:20.188 --> 00:51:20.768
Who'll be next?

00:51:22.268 --> 00:51:22.868
How will it happen?

00:51:24.732 --> 00:51:26.332
Let me ask you a question, Doctor.

00:51:27.452 --> 00:51:29.332
You were the first one to see my wife there.

00:51:30.348 --> 00:51:33.108
Did you also see anything that she could have climbed up on?

00:51:33.420 --> 00:51:34.220
and then jumped.

00:51:34.540 --> 00:51:34.960
No.

00:51:36.556 --> 00:51:37.256
Did any of you?

00:51:41.420 --> 00:51:42.140
There was nothing.

00:51:43.852 --> 00:51:45.852
How then did she get up there?

00:51:45.868 --> 00:51:46.868
so high.

00:51:46.956 --> 00:51:48.576
Exactly, Mr. Loren. How?

00:51:49.260 --> 00:51:50.740
She couldn't have pulled herself up there.

00:51:50.840 --> 00:51:52.220
She couldn't have dropped from the ceiling.

00:51:53.676 --> 00:51:55.176
Do you think your wife killed herself?

00:51:56.812 --> 00:51:57.652
No.

00:51:58.348 --> 00:51:59.188
She was murdered.

00:52:00.960 --> 00:52:13.740
by one of you for you mr lauren to deliberately kill someone you must have a reason we were all

00:52:13.740 --> 00:52:21.420
strangers to your wife only you had a motive for murder my husband hasn't it sometime wanted to kill

00:52:21.420 --> 00:52:26.620
his wife what husband hasn't had a thousand opportunities to do it in such a way so that

00:52:26.620 --> 00:52:29.860
he'd never be suspected i'm not such a fool as to hang my

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:31.700
from a ceiling, by a rope.

00:52:32.040 --> 00:52:35.640
The fact remains that you, or one of us, murdered Mrs. Lauren.

00:52:36.460 --> 00:52:37.680
And that's a matter for the police.

00:52:37.920 --> 00:52:39.360
So how do we get the police?

00:52:39.780 --> 00:52:41.920
That's my point. We can't until morning.

00:52:43.130 --> 00:52:45.290
What began as a silly party given by an eccentric

00:52:45.290 --> 00:52:47.190
has now involved us all in murder.

00:52:48.180 --> 00:52:49.560
For once, Pritchard may be right.

00:52:50.120 --> 00:52:52.340
If another murder's in the works, let's stop it now.

00:52:52.800 --> 00:52:53.680
Another murder?

00:52:54.410 --> 00:52:57.300
Why not? Maybe one of us saw too much.

00:53:00.800 --> 00:53:06.260
Why should even a millionaire want to give each of us $10,000 to spend one night in a gloomy old house?

00:53:06.630 --> 00:53:08.370
To see some ghosts, to have a party?

00:53:09.330 --> 00:53:09.710
No.

00:53:10.110 --> 00:53:11.430
Have you finished trying me, doctor?

00:53:11.760 --> 00:53:13.500
And is the verdict guilty of murder?

00:53:14.040 --> 00:53:15.600
Oh, this isn't getting us anywhere.

00:53:15.800 --> 00:53:17.640
Somebody killed Mrs. Lauren, we know that.

00:53:18.260 --> 00:53:20.120
One of us is guilty and the rest of us are innocent.

00:53:20.260 --> 00:53:20.520
Okay.

00:53:21.310 --> 00:53:25.340
Now, what we have to do for the next six hours is protect ourselves from each other.

00:53:26.200 --> 00:53:27.660
Do you really think...

00:53:27.660 --> 00:53:28.640
I don't think anything.

00:53:29.330 --> 00:53:29.970
I just know...

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:30.920
and I'm going to my room.

00:53:31.220 --> 00:53:34.760
And if anybody comes in, I'll shoot him or her.

00:53:35.110 --> 00:53:37.110
And if we all stay in our rooms, we'll be safe

00:53:37.110 --> 00:53:40.060
because the innocent will have no reason to leave his room

00:53:40.060 --> 00:53:43.140
and the guilty will admit his guilt if he or she does.

00:53:43.660 --> 00:53:44.760
And we all have guns.

00:53:45.420 --> 00:53:46.140
We're all agreed.

00:53:47.640 --> 00:53:49.620
Oh, I wish this night were over.

00:53:52.700 --> 00:53:53.100
Rooms?

00:53:56.180 --> 00:53:57.780
I tell you, it doesn't make any difference.

00:53:59.180 --> 00:53:59.880
They aren't through.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:00.540
with our share.

00:54:31.950 --> 00:54:33.470
What's the use of saying goodnight?

00:55:08.990 --> 00:55:09.470
Good night, doctor.

00:57:34.960 --> 00:57:35.520
Me, Lance.

00:57:41.790 --> 00:57:42.110
Okay.

00:57:44.110 --> 00:57:45.990
They've all gone to their rooms and locked themselves in.

00:57:46.530 --> 00:57:47.410
Lance, I've been thinking.

00:57:48.060 --> 00:57:49.120
It was so dark down there.

00:57:49.160 --> 00:57:50.360
Maybe it wasn't Mr. Lord.

00:57:51.360 --> 00:57:52.060
It was him, all right.

00:57:52.640 --> 00:57:54.500
Tried to kill you, and he did kill his wife.

00:57:54.680 --> 00:57:58.180
How can you be so sure?

00:57:58.900 --> 00:57:59.600
He tried to warn me.

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:00.800
Ask me to help her.

00:58:02.340 --> 00:58:04.200
The doc thinks he's going to try and kill one of us.

00:58:06.780 --> 00:58:07.880
Must be a way out of this place,

00:58:07.920 --> 00:58:10.040
and I'm going to find it and get the police before he does.

00:58:10.680 --> 00:58:11.500
I'm going with you.

00:58:12.360 --> 00:58:13.740
If he finds out you're alive...

00:58:15.170 --> 00:58:17.620
No, Nora, you're safer here than anyplace else.

00:58:18.060 --> 00:58:19.660
Now just lock yourself in and keep quiet.

00:59:01.010 --> 00:59:01.070
Thank you.

01:01:01.660 --> 01:01:01.840
Thank you.

01:02:50.410 --> 01:02:57.280
certainly not there's either somebody else in this house or one of us has left his room did you hear

01:02:57.280 --> 01:02:57.480
anything

01:03:01.980 --> 01:03:02.660
Organ music?

01:03:03.150 --> 01:03:05.160
That, and someone walking.

01:03:07.640 --> 01:03:08.500
Got yours ready?

01:03:12.140 --> 01:03:14.330
You look downstairs, and I'll look up here.

01:03:15.070 --> 01:03:15.770
Why not together?

01:03:16.420 --> 01:03:18.640
There may be only minutes, seconds left of someone's life.

01:03:19.300 --> 01:03:20.100
Why waste time?

01:04:15.000 --> 01:04:15.680
It's almost over, darling.

01:04:18.280 --> 01:04:19.580
Every detail was perfect.

01:04:31.850 --> 01:04:34.860
What's happening?

01:04:35.970 --> 01:04:36.650
We've done it.

01:04:37.640 --> 01:04:38.360
Perfect crime.

01:04:42.220 --> 01:04:42.920
Has she killed him?

01:04:43.890 --> 01:04:45.760
Not yet, but she will.

01:04:49.160 --> 01:04:50.640
Get me out of this hanging harness.

01:04:52.870 --> 01:04:54.130
What's taking that girl so long?

01:04:54.170 --> 01:04:54.830
What time is it?

01:04:55.820 --> 01:04:58.240
First, I couldn't get Nora to want to protect herself with a gun.

01:04:58.940 --> 01:04:59.960
After you appeared at the window...

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:04.460
everything began to work just as we had planned you were wonderful just the touch that finally

01:05:04.460 --> 01:05:11.140
drove her into complete hysteria it'll be worth all of our planning darling where's nora now what's

01:05:11.800 --> 01:05:17.460
happening on the way to the cellar so scared she'll shoot the first thing that moves and frederick

01:05:17.460 --> 01:05:25.240
on his way to the cellar too david are you sure none of them will suspect us of what an hysterical

01:05:25.240 --> 01:05:29.180
girl accidentally shoots somebody who would suspect that we planned it that way that we drove her to

01:05:29.180 --> 01:05:29.970
What a f**k.

01:05:30.820 --> 01:05:35.420
Just a ghost party gag. We'll claim it was a dummy since I'm the only one who touched you.

01:05:35.910 --> 01:05:36.650
And the caretakers?

01:05:37.840 --> 01:05:39.360
Well, they had no idea what they were really doing.

01:05:39.880 --> 01:05:41.740
What about Nora? She's not stupid, you know.

01:05:41.840 --> 01:05:44.700
Darling, believe me, everything we've planned is working perfectly.

01:05:45.710 --> 01:05:47.270
Nora is sure Frederick murdered you.

01:05:47.650 --> 01:05:49.490
She thinks Frederick attacked her in the cellar, not me.

01:05:50.020 --> 01:05:51.900
And now Nora's almost out of her mind with fear.

01:05:52.300 --> 01:05:53.500
The heads, the music you're hanging,

01:05:53.740 --> 01:05:55.680
I tell you when Frederick walks in there, she'll shoot him.

01:05:56.940 --> 01:05:59.980
Taking too long. David, you ought to be there.

01:06:10.590 --> 01:06:12.980
When you hear the shot, come down to the center.

01:08:35.530 --> 01:08:54.000
David? David?

01:10:31.500 --> 01:10:34.000
You're not going to live to enjoy it.

01:10:34.470 --> 01:10:36.130
Come with me, murderess.

01:10:36.680 --> 01:10:37.840
Come with me.

01:12:05.308 --> 01:12:05.808
about.

01:12:07.900 --> 01:12:10.900
The time you two planned was indeed perfect.

01:12:11.548 --> 01:12:14.308
Only the victim is alive and the murderers are not.

01:12:16.220 --> 01:12:18.980
A pity you didn't know when you started your game of murder.

01:12:21.052 --> 01:12:22.452
that I was playing too.

01:12:28.956 --> 01:12:29.996
There must be some way to get in.

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:32.000
It's right along here, somewhere.

01:12:36.940 --> 01:12:39.300
I've shot Mr. Lorne. He's down in the wine cellar.

01:12:40.236 --> 01:12:40.676
Alive.

01:12:40.972 --> 01:12:41.812
I don't think so.

01:12:53.420 --> 01:12:53.960
He's alive.

01:13:00.252 --> 01:13:02.252
I didn't shoot anyone, my dear.

01:13:02.524 --> 01:13:04.264
I loaded your gun with blanks.

01:13:06.012 --> 01:13:07.252
I can tell you all now.

01:13:08.316 --> 01:13:10.276
Trent and my wife were planning to kill me.

01:13:11.548 --> 01:13:12.208
They failed.

01:13:13.948 --> 01:13:15.528
Trent tried to throw me in the vat.

01:13:16.668 --> 01:13:18.208
My wife stumbled and fell.

01:13:20.476 --> 01:13:22.976
I'm ready for justice to decide if I'm...

01:13:23.324 --> 01:13:24.204
Innocent or.

01:13:25.212 --> 01:13:25.572
guilty.

01:13:49.772 --> 01:13:50.772
There will be more, many more.

01:13:55.948 --> 01:13:56.748
for me now.

01:14:00.730 --> 01:14:02.350
And then they'll come for you.
